(5273895, 765704, 49109, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon and new PB. Great sense of dynamics here, reminds me of my own shot <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=623500" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/788/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_623500.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/788/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_623500.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/788/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_623500.jpg"/></a>, but yours is far more interesting</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon and new PB. Great sense of dynamics here, reminds me of my own shot , but yours is far more interesting', '2009-02-25 07:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273911, 765724, 58691, '<td valign="top">Congrats on another ribbon Andrew,</td>', 'Congrats on another ribbon Andrew,', '2009-02-25 08:02:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273915, 765091, 99218, '<td valign="top">Fantastic awesome shot!</td>', 'Fantastic awesome shot!', '2009-02-25 08:04:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273924, 765704, 99218, '<td valign="top">Awesome!</td>', 'Awesome!', '2009-02-25 08:09:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273930, 765005, 1858, '<td valign="top">Silly me; I thought it said title, not tilted.</td>', 'Silly me; I thought it said title, not tilted.', '2009-02-25 08:11:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273933, 766103, 73235, '<td valign="top">6th place!!! Congratulations.</td>', '6th place!!! Congratulations.', '2009-02-25 08:12:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273940, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top">Post Rating:<br/> <br/>I sent a question to DPC admin seeking clarification about the requirements of this challenge before setting out with camera in hand.<br/> <br/>I asked whether the challenge is restricted to stereotypic, rotated-camera outdoor, landscape pictures.  I was told no.<br/> <br/>I asked whether an indoor picture which includes one or more structural, horizontal lines - which emulate the horizon -meet the requirements of the challenge.  I was told yes.<br/> <br/>I was further told that such an indoor picture is entirely consistent with the ''imaginative'' use of a tilted horizon.<br/> <br/>In the photo, the white roof girders emulate the horizon being level ordinarily.  This roof is massive, covering more than 9 acres.<br/> <br/>Having thusly met the requirements of the challenge, I  confess, I was a little disappointed in the scores voters gave. <br/> <br/> I thought the facial expressions of the adventurers on the Plunge were well captured and telegraphed their experiences in surviving the many-times-tilted horizon which this ride offers.<br/></td>', 'Post Rating: I sent a question to DPC admin seeking clarification about the requirements of this challenge before setting out with camera in hand. I asked whether the challenge is restricted to stereotypic, rotated-camera outdoor, landscape pictures.  I was told no. I asked whether an indoor picture which includes one or more structural, horizontal lines - which emulate the horizon -meet the requirements of the challenge.  I was told yes. I was further told that such an indoor picture is entirely consistent with the ''imaginative'' use of a tilted horizon. In the photo, the white roof girders emulate the horizon being level ordinarily.  This roof is massive, covering more than 9 acres. Having thusly met the requirements of the challenge, I  confess, I was a little disappointed in the scores voters gave.   I thought the facial expressions of the adventurers on the Plunge were well captured and telegraphed their experiences in surviving the many-times-tilted horizon which this ride offers.', '2009-02-25 08:15:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273946, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mikeee:</b></div><hr/><i> Great expressions, but the subjects are slightly OOF. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The car and riders were approaching the camera head on at about 50 miles an hour and turned sharply to the right about 20 feet in front of the camera.  The car and riders were relatively dark, the lighting being overpowered by the tilted, transparent roof windows.  Neither my camera nor I could achieve the exposure quickly enough, and some softening of the focus occured.  Next time I will use different camera settings.  Thanks for your comment.</td>', 'Originally posted by mikeee: Great expressions, but the subjects are slightly OOF.   The car and riders were approaching the camera head on at about 50 miles an hour and turned sharply to the right about 20 feet in front of the camera.  The car and riders were relatively dark, the lighting being overpowered by the tilted, transparent roof windows.  Neither my camera nor I could achieve the exposure quickly enough, and some softening of the focus occured.  Next time I will use different camera settings.  Thanks for your comment.', '2009-02-25 08:21:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273948, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LanceW:</b></div><hr/><i> There''s no horizon in this photo... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-25 08:27:22.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LanceW: There''s no horizon in this photo...   Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.', '2009-02-25 08:22:24.000000', '2009-02-25 08:27:22.000000', 0),
(5273949, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Fun shot.  But I find the lighting overall to be flat and uninteresting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Please see Photogher''s Comments for a description of the lighting available in this venue; flashes not allowed.</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Fun shot.  But I find the lighting overall to be flat and uninteresting.   Please see Photogher''s Comments for a description of the lighting available in this venue; flashes not allowed.', '2009-02-25 08:24:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273951, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> "...submit a shot with a TILTED horizon used effectively."<br/> <br/>I don''t see a horizon at all here.   <br/> <br/>Cool, fun shot though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-25 08:26:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: "...submit a shot with a TILTED horizon used effectively." I don''t see a horizon at all here.    Cool, fun shot though.   Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.', '2009-02-25 08:25:05.000000', '2009-02-25 08:26:56.000000', 0),
(5273954, 765992, 42091, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by orvaratli:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a nice image but the connection with the challenge is weak. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-02-25 08:26:20.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by orvaratli: This is a nice image but the connection with the challenge is weak.   Please see my summary of information provided by DPC regarding this.', '2009-02-25 08:25:32.000000', '2009-02-25 08:26:20.000000', 0),
(5273966, 765332, 72670, '<td valign="top">Hey Brad<br/>Congrats on the top ten finish. Great shot.Looks like you and Johnathan<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=81530" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jeger</a> were on a date again. :)</td>', 'Hey BradCongrats on the top ten finish. Great shot.Looks like you and Johnathan jeger were on a date again. :)', '2009-02-25 08:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5273967, 765724, 87808, '<td valign="top">Dammmmmmmmn I gave this a 9.  lol, well done on beating me and having an amazing score</td>', 'Dammmmmmmmn I gave this a 9.  lol, well done on beating me and having an amazing score', '2009-02-25 08:33:22.000000', NULL, 0),
