(5275370, 765738, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>well seen--achieving a tilted horizon without tilting.  I like the way you think.<br/>A bit of a crop up from the bottom and down from the top would enhance the surrealistic possibilities</td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee!well seen--achieving a tilted horizon without tilting.  I like the way you think.A bit of a crop up from the bottom and down from the top would enhance the surrealistic possibilities', '2009-02-25 23:39:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275373, 766073, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>beautiful composition, use of negative space, and it somehow makes the tilt seem natural, unforced, and not at all disorienting....<br/>well done</td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee!beautiful composition, use of negative space, and it somehow makes the tilt seem natural, unforced, and not at all disorienting....well done', '2009-02-25 23:41:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275375, 765968, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award Nominee!<br/>beautiful luminous tones and wonderful conversion, well composed</td>', 'PostLuminous Award Nominee!beautiful luminous tones and wonderful conversion, well composed', '2009-02-25 23:43:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275385, 765884, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677020" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg"/></a>PostLuminous Award WINNER!<br/>This is a superb image, slightly surreal, tilt used to great effect, and a beautifully luminous conversion/tonality.</td>', 'PostLuminous Award WINNER!This is a superb image, slightly surreal, tilt used to great effect, and a beautifully luminous conversion/tonality.', '2009-02-25 23:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275423, 765659, 43679, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the nice comments.  I do get that the horizon isn''t tilted technically, but wanted to do something a bit unique for the challenge.  And, due to the "no healing brush" rule, I couldn''t clean up the raw edge of the posterboard against the background.<br/> <br/>Setup shot is at <a href="//www.woodstonephoto.com/blog/2009/02/tilt.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.woodstonephoto.com/blog/2009/02/tilt.html</a> if anyone''s interested.  I incidentally used the glass-on-a-pole as a beverage scepter for Mardi Gras. :)</td>', 'Thanks all for the nice comments.  I do get that the horizon isn''t tilted technically, but wanted to do something a bit unique for the challenge.  And, due to the "no healing brush" rule, I couldn''t clean up the raw edge of the posterboard against the background. Setup shot is at //www.woodstonephoto.com/blog/2009/02/tilt.html if anyone''s interested.  I incidentally used the glass-on-a-pole as a beverage scepter for Mardi Gras. :)', '2009-02-26 00:19:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275688, 766065, 30982, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Irene!  Not only on the Yellow Hand, and a cool shot, but the opportunity to watch the swan break the ice in the first place.  AND the opportunity to make your husband wonder just a bit about your sanity and the whole Yellow Hand bit.</td>', 'Congratulations Irene!  Not only on the Yellow Hand, and a cool shot, but the opportunity to watch the swan break the ice in the first place.  AND the opportunity to make your husband wonder just a bit about your sanity and the whole Yellow Hand bit.', '2009-02-26 08:20:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275856, 765724, 2553, '<td valign="top">I didn''t enter this challenge because I really tend to hate tilted horizons, but this image certainly proves to be the exception!  Awesome, well-done shot, and congratulations!</td>', 'I didn''t enter this challenge because I really tend to hate tilted horizons, but this image certainly proves to be the exception!  Awesome, well-done shot, and congratulations!', '2009-02-26 09:53:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5275978, 765091, 39427, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Physics_McG:</b></div><hr/><i> I just don''t get the whole border deal.....it just takes so much away from the picture as far as being up close and personal with the subject. I can''t say whether the picture is good or not because of the lack of detail. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The "Image" part of the submission would not be any larger, and you would not be able to see any more detail if the border wasn''t there, as it is cropped @640px as per basic editing rules.  Without the frame, the image just looks too wide for me, which is why I put it in there to stabilize the shot and have some black to contrast against, instead of the grey of the DPC viewing pages.  Of course its just a personal thing, I just happen to like how it looks.</td>', 'Originally posted by Physics_McG: I just don''t get the whole border deal.....it just takes so much away from the picture as far as being up close and personal with the subject. I can''t say whether the picture is good or not because of the lack of detail.   The "Image" part of the submission would not be any larger, and you would not be able to see any more detail if the border wasn''t there, as it is cropped @640px as per basic editing rules.  Without the frame, the image just looks too wide for me, which is why I put it in there to stabilize the shot and have some black to contrast against, instead of the grey of the DPC viewing pages.  Of course its just a personal thing, I just happen to like how it looks.', '2009-02-26 11:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
