(5278572, 765091, 4494, '<td valign="top">I think what makes this image so great is not just the absolutely perfect colors, but the great "balance" of all the parts.  The bridge and the water is perfectly balanced in the pic which makes the "tilted" concept work great because you don''t feel like anything is out of whack.  Awesome!<br/></td>', 'I think what makes this image so great is not just the absolutely perfect colors, but the great "balance" of all the parts.  The bridge and the water is perfectly balanced in the pic which makes the "tilted" concept work great because you don''t feel like anything is out of whack.  Awesome!', '2009-02-27 22:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5278897, 766167, 67697, '<td valign="top">I wrote a comment and it never posted - how annoying!  I have to say that I did not get a sense of tilt from the book.  Maybe because the area before the book is so dark?  For me, there is no reference horizon that would give me a clue about the position of the book.  I can see where the glasses are at a slight angle but it just makes me think of one of those books that are hard to keep closed.  I like the yellowish sepia-tone color - makes me think of one who is trying to read in the dark using only candlelight.</td>', 'I wrote a comment and it never posted - how annoying!  I have to say that I did not get a sense of tilt from the book.  Maybe because the area before the book is so dark?  For me, there is no reference horizon that would give me a clue about the position of the book.  I can see where the glasses are at a slight angle but it just makes me think of one of those books that are hard to keep closed.  I like the yellowish sepia-tone color - makes me think of one who is trying to read in the dark using only candlelight.', '2009-02-28 10:09:04.000000', NULL, 0),
